Report every video decrypt failure to the observer, rate-limited, independent
of failure_tolerance.

FrameCryptorTransformer::decryptFrame() only ever notifies the observer of a
decryption failure through ParticipantKeyHandler::DecryptionFailure(), which
is a hard no-op (returns false unconditionally, notifying nothing) whenever
KeyProviderOptions.failure_tolerance is left at its default of -1. Raising
failure_tolerance app-side is not a fix: past the threshold the handler marks
itself invalid and freezes the receiver until a full rekey, which is worse
than today's silence. The practical effect on the Android E2EE video path:
a plain AES-GCM tag mismatch (the common case after a storm-induced epoch
skew, or a frame decoded against a just-retired key slot) produced ZERO
signal - no observer callback, nothing an app-level keyframe-request policy
could react to - until a generic multi-second wire-level watchdog eventually
noticed frames had stopped rendering.

This adds a second, unconditional notification path at the same call site:
a decrypt failure now always posts FrameCryptionState::kDecryptionFailed to
the observer, rate-limited to at most once per 250ms per transformer via a
lock-free atomic timestamp CAS (decryptFrame() does not hold the transformer
mutex_ at this call site, and a relaxed compare_exchange is exactly the
"try to become the one notifier this window" pattern this needs - losing the
race just means a concurrent decrypt already claimed the window). It never
reads or writes has_valid_key_/decryption_failure_count_, so every existing
failure_tolerance/ratchet-freeze semantics for callers that DO set a positive
tolerance are byte-for-byte unchanged; the two notification paths below now
simply coexist, and observers already dedupe on their own (e.g.
CallController's WIRE_SPEC keyframe-request path rate-limits to 1/s
independent of this).

diff --git a/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.h b/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.h
index 6d01653..a1e5c40 100644
--- a/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.h
+++ b/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.h
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #ifndef WEBRTC_FRAME_CRYPTOR_TRANSFORMER_H_
 #define WEBRTC_FRAME_CRYPTOR_TRANSFORMER_H_
 
+#include <atomic>
 #include <unordered_map>
 
 #include "api/frame_transformer_interface.h"
@@ -490,6 +491,11 @@
   webrtc::scoped_refptr<FrameCryptorTransformerObserver> observer_;
   FrameCryptionState last_enc_error_ = FrameCryptionState::kNew;
   FrameCryptionState last_dec_error_ = FrameCryptionState::kNew;
+  // W-NATIVEPLI (2026-08-25): last time an UNCONDITIONAL decrypt-failure
+  // notification fired (see decryptFrame()'s doc in the .cc). Deliberately
+  // separate from last_dec_error_ above, which the pre-existing
+  // failure_tolerance-gated path still owns unchanged.
+  std::atomic<int64_t> last_decrypt_fail_notify_ms_{0};
 };
 
 class RTC_EXPORT EncryptedPacket : public webrtc::RefCountInterface {
diff --git a/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc b/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc
index 1111111..2222222 100644
